    <h1>{{ site.name }}</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">{{ site.title }} | {{ site.institution }}</p>

    <p class="banner-question">
      When an AI says it's &ldquo;thinking,&rdquo; what is it actually doing? Is it reasoning, or performing?
      Can it be manipulated &mdash; and is it manipulating us?
    </p>

    <p>
      I build and evaluate AI reasoning you can <strong>inspect</strong>, <strong>contest</strong>, and
      <strong>trust</strong>. My work spans adversarial evaluation of reasoning and agentic systems,
      computational argumentation, uncertainty quantification, and machine theory of mind. At Leidos, I
      lead a research team building secure agentic AI &mdash; verification systems that decompose model
      outputs into claims, evidence, assumptions, and uncertainty, so reasoning failures get caught
      before they reach high-stakes decisions.
    </p>

    <p>
      Before AI, I spent nearly a decade as an intellectual property attorney at
      <a href="https://www.ropesgray.com/en">Ropes &amp; Gray</a>. Law is adversarial reasoning as a
      profession &mdash; evidence, argument, cross-examination, bad-faith persuasion &mdash; and I bring
      that toolkit to stress-testing AI systems that act. More on the questions I'm working on:
      <a href="/research/">Research</a>.
    </p>

